Story/Characters/The%20Inheritor.md\">The Inheritor</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"confirmed-facts-and-current-working-constraints\">Confirmed facts and current working constraints</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants enter functioning reconstructed societies with incomplete knowledge.</li>\n<li>Current channel note describes infancy formation and later conscious awakening.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These constraints inherit their source status. A working physical model, timing estimate, or accepted macro constraint does not establish every implementation detail.</p>\n<h4 id=\"unresolved-gaps-and-contradictions\">Unresolved gaps and contradictions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Exact pre-entry briefing, memory withholding, re-entry, convicted-participant review, and locally born descendants. Voluntary heir entry and exit are now established.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"prerequisite-decisions\">Prerequisite decisions</h4>\n<p>Modules: 01. Read their accepted results before closing this gate. Open prerequisites can be explored provisionally, but do not mark dependent choices final. Module numbers are topic IDs; use the dependency order in the workshop index.</p>\n<h4 id=\"central-author-gate\">Central author gate</h4>\n<blockquote>What did each class of participant knowingly accept before entry, and what can they refuse afterward? <strong>PARTIALLY AUTHOR-ACCEPTED 2026-09-06:</strong> voluntary heirs and trainees are settled; convicted participants and descendants retain separate open mechanics.</blockquote>\n<p>Ask this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.</p>\n<h4 id=\"possibilities-and-tradeoffs\">Possibilities and tradeoffs</h4>\n<h5 id=\"1-informed-consent-to-a-bounded-unknown\">1. Informed consent to a bounded unknown</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Participants accept broad risks and protected exit without learning scenario details. Preserves discovery and agency; requires a believable consent memory or trusted independent record.</p>\n<h5 id=\"2-ordinary-upbringing-followed-by-renewed-participation-choice\">2. Ordinary upbringing followed by renewed participation choice</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> The childhood bond is developmental background, while conscious adulthood creates the first binding training choice. Strong human formation; must explain what a refusal permits and whether refusal damages placement.</p>\n<h5 id=\"3-court-assigned-containment-separately-consented-training\">3. Court-assigned containment, separately consented training</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Criminal jurisdiction and trainee participation follow different routes. Clarifies responsibility but creates multiple knowledge tracks that need simple reader cues.</p>\n<h5 id=\"4-contested-entry-practice-requiring-reform\">4. Contested entry practice requiring reform</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Some withholding proves excessive and Sylvan challenges it. Gives leaders fallibility and a personal conflict; changes the positive civilization from established ethical model to institution under repair.</p>\n<h4 id=\"targeted-follow-up-questions\">Targeted follow-up questions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Can a participant leave without confessing failure?</li>\n<li>Can parents authorize what their adult child later rejects?</li>\n<li>What do descendants born inside the process inherit: circumstances, permissions, or obligations?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"scene-test\">Scene test</h4>\n<p><strong>Non-canon situation:</strong> At awakening Sylvan asks what he agreed to; the Luminai can produce only part of the answer, so a real choice must occur before the next stage.</p>\n<p>Record what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.</p>\n<h4 id=\"adversarial-questions\">Adversarial questions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Does uncertainty conceal the scenario, or conceal rights a person would need to exercise consent?</li>\n<li>Which established constraint would this answer break, and what evidence would reveal that break before the payoff?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"completion-checklist\">Completion checklist</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>☑ Answer the central question in the author&#x27;s own words for voluntary heirs and trainees.</li>\n<li>☑ Identify the chosen possibility, a modified combination, or a different answer; explain rejected tradeoffs.</li>\n<li>☑ Resolve prerequisite 01.</li>\n<li>☑ Run the scene test above and state the consequence for the people involved.</li>\n<li>☑ Answer the adversarial challenge without granting unexplained knowledge or authority.</li>\n<li>☑ Record what remains working, proposed, or unresolved.</li>\n<li>☑ Obtain explicit author acceptance before updating canon or workflow progress.</li>\n<li>☑ Trace the accepted answer through the affected notes and rebuild both projections.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"answer-and-decision-record\">Answer and decision record</h4>\n<pre><code>Module: 02 · Participant knowledge and entry\nGate: What did each class of participant knowingly accept before entry, and what can they refuse afterward?\nState: AUTHOR-ACCEPTED for voluntary heirs and trainees; other classes explicitly deferred\nAuthor answer (verbatim): preserved in the linked session record\nExact restatement: accepted result above\nSelected option or new answer: voluntary opportunity with a continuing right to exit and return to inheritance\nWhy this tradeoff: the process offers an independently earned future instead of compulsory preparation for inherited power\nRejected alternatives and reasons: criminal release and descendant obligations cannot be inferred from the heir model\nPrerequisites resolved / deferred: Module 01 resolved\nScene test: an heir may leave after a setback but gives up the unfinished process result; a convicted participant requires a different legal route\nAdversarial result: exit does not erase stakes because inheritance and independently earned placement are different futures\nRemaining uncertainty: exact briefing, traded results, re-entry, stage refusal, criminal review and descendant rights\nExplicit acceptance wording and date: “Yes, another great result, the improvements are good” — 2026-09-06\nWorkflow task and macro-depth effect: supporting workshop Module 02 accepted for voluntary entrants; SC-010 remains active and unchanged</code></pre>\n<h4 id=\"notes-and-website-sections-affected\">Notes and website sections affected</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/01%20Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05%20-%20Integrated%20Foundation%20Audit%20and%20Workshop%20Build.md\">2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Components/Learned%20Wireless%20Cognitive%20Channel.md\">Learned Wireless Cognitive Channel</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Characters/The%20Inheritor.md\">The Inheritor</a></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Public atlas: <code>docs/colonization.html</code>, the matching source in <code>05 Public/Atlas/</code>, and the workshop projection.</li>\n<li>Development Explorer: the relevant topic view, this source packet, and linked evidence/decision records.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20QA/Decisions.md\">Decisions</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20QA/Questions.md\">Questions</a>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20Coordination/Weekly%20Synthesis/CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE.md\">CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE</a>. Update <a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20Coordination/CURRENT-PICKUP.md\">CURRENT-PICKUP</a> and the current task only if the author accepts a workflow-relevant decision.</li>\n</ul>"
