      "path": "07 Coordination/Story Completion Workflow/Workshop/05 - Luminai generations and causal comparison.md",
      "markdown": "---\ntype: workshop-module\nstatus: proposed-options-author-gate-open\nmodule: 05\ntitle: Luminai generations and causal comparison\ngate: What new capacity does deeper integration supply that must still be governed by human choices and institutions?\nprerequisites: 01, 02, 04\nupdated: 2026-09-05\n---\n\n# 05 · Luminai generations and causal comparison\n\n## Purpose\n\nDefine the technical difference without making newer cognition automatically virtuous.\n\nThis packet supports the existing Story Completion Workflow. It does not advance a checklist or settle canon. All alternatives below are PROPOSED; the gate is OPEN. Central synthesis: Astra, reviewed for integration on September 5.\n\n## Relevant source notes\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Human–Luminai Pairing and Bonding]]\n- [[02 Story/Components/Bridge World and Luminai Initialization]]\n\n## Confirmed facts and current working constraints\n\n- Earlier participants used earlier Luminai; daemon identifies an evil soul, not age.\n- Sylvan is the first complete real-world test of the deeper successor integration.\n\nThese constraints inherit their source status. A working physical model, timing estimate, or accepted macro constraint does not establish every implementation detail.\n\n## Unresolved gaps and contradictions\n\n- Which capacity changes; whether malicious deeply integrated people remain possible; what evidence distinguishes architecture from Sylvan’s character.\n\n## Prerequisite decisions\n\nModules: 01, 02, 04. Read their accepted results before closing this gate. Open prerequisites can be explored provisionally, but do not mark dependent choices final. Module numbers are topic IDs; use the dependency order in the workshop index.\n\n## Central author gate\n\n> What new capacity does deeper integration supply that must still be governed by human choices and institutions?\n\nAsk this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.\n\n## Possibilities and tradeoffs\n\n### 1. Richer reciprocal error correction\n\n**PROPOSED:** The pair detects mismatch between prediction, experience and consequence sooner. Useful against performed obedience; it can still entrench shared mistakes without outside evidence.\n\n### 2. Finer provenance and intention differentiation\n\n**PROPOSED:** The pair can distinguish source, inference and conscious authorization. Supports evidence thriller; not truth detection and not immunity to persuasive false context.\n\n### 3. Broader embodied environmental coordination\n\n**PROPOSED:** The pair learns to act across physical systems with less translation. Offers vivid competence and costs; power alone says nothing about ethical use.\n\n### 4. More stable revision across long experience\n\n**PROPOSED:** The pair can update goals and self-models without identity collapse. Strong foil to Konrad; requires costly episodes where Sylvan revises a cherished premise instead of software doing it for him.\n\n## Targeted follow-up questions\n\n- Show an older healthy Luminai succeeding at an ethical act: what remains valid in the older generation?\n- Show the new bond making a confident error: who corrects it?\n- Which result supports wider testing, rather than proving the new generation morally superior?\n\n## Scene test\n\n**Non-canon situation:** Konrad’s daemon solves a difficult tactical problem accurately; Sylvan’s new bond misreads a person, and Sylvan must accept external correction.\n\nRecord what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.\n\n## Adversarial questions\n\n- Would deeper integration with Samuel make him a better human—or a more coherent manipulator? If the latter is possible, what real safeguard changes the result?\n- Which established constraint would this answer break, and what evidence would reveal that break before the payoff?\n\n## Completion checklist\n\n- [ ] Answer the central question in the author's own words.\n- [ ] Identify the chosen possibility, a modified combination, or a different answer; explain rejected tradeoffs.\n- [ ] Resolve or explicitly defer prerequisites 01, 02, 04.\n- [ ] Run the scene test above and state the consequence for the people involved.\n- [ ] Answer the adversarial challenge without granting unexplained knowledge or authority.\n- [ ] Record what remains working, proposed, or unresolved.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit author acceptance before updating canon or workflow progress.\n- [ ] Trace the accepted answer through the affected notes and rebuild both projections.\n\n## Answer and decision record\n\n```text\nModule: 05 · Luminai generations and causal comparison\nGate: What new capacity does deeper integration supply that must still be governed by human choices and institutions?\nState: DRAFT / PROPOSED / AUTHOR-ACCEPTED / REJECTED / DEFERRED\nAuthor answer (verbatim):\nExact restatement:\nSelected option or new answer:\nWhy this tradeoff:\nRejected alternatives and reasons:\nPrerequisites resolved / deferred:\nScene test: choices, permissions, evidence, cost:\nAdversarial result:\nRemaining uncertainty:\nExplicit acceptance wording and date:\nAffected notes updated:\nQA decision reference:\nWorkflow task and macro-depth effect:\nWebsite rebuild and verification:\n```\n\n## Notes and website sections affected\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Human–Luminai Pairing and Bonding]]\n- [[02 Story/Components/Bridge World and Luminai Initialization]]\n\n- Public atlas: `docs/ai.html`, the matching source in `05 Public/Atlas/`, and the workshop projection.\n- Development Explorer: the relevant topic view, this source packet, and linked evidence/decision records.\n- [[07 QA/Decisions]], [[07 QA/Questions]], and [[07 Coordination/Weekly Synthesis/CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE]]. Update [[07 Coordination/CURRENT-PICKUP]] and the current task only if the author accepts a workflow-relevant decision.\n",
