      "markdown": "---\ntype: workshop-module\nstatus: proposed-options-author-gate-open\nmodule: 09\ntitle: Great War defeat and refusal to exit\ngate: What exactly would lawful exit have done to Konrad’s authority and to the people under him?\nprerequisites: 02, 03, 08\nupdated: 2026-09-05\n---\n\n# 09 · Great War defeat and refusal to exit\n\n## Purpose\n\nMake the historical hinge a real choice with a defined lawful alternative.\n\nThis packet supports the existing Story Completion Workflow. It does not advance a checklist or settle canon. All alternatives below are PROPOSED; the gate is OPEN. Central synthesis: Astra, reviewed for integration on September 5.\n\n## Relevant source notes\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/Konrad Fitzgerald]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Participant Governance and Command Rules]]\n\n## Confirmed facts and current working constraints\n\n- Konrad’s experiment should end after defeat.\n- He chooses continued participation and reactivation to vindicate his ideology and daemon.\n\nThese constraints inherit their source status. A working physical model, timing estimate, or accepted macro constraint does not establish every implementation detail.\n\n## Unresolved gaps and contradictions\n\n- Exit destination and sentence; individual versus collective choice; ability to refuse while remaining contained.\n\n## Prerequisite decisions\n\nModules: 02, 03, 08. Read their accepted results before closing this gate. Open prerequisites can be explored provisionally, but do not mark dependent choices final. Module numbers are topic IDs; use the dependency order in the workshop index.\n\n## Central author gate\n\n> What exactly would lawful exit have done to Konrad’s authority and to the people under him?\n\nAsk this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.\n\n## Possibilities and tradeoffs\n\n### 1. End command, continue individual review elsewhere\n\n**PROPOSED:** Konrad leaves his governance role and faces ordinary adjudication; followers receive separate assessments. Clear distinction from freedom or absolution; requires another holding context.\n\n### 2. Disband faction jurisdiction, retain bounded personal participation\n\n**PROPOSED:** Konrad could remain as an individual but rejects loss of corporate authority. Concentrates motive on domination; explain how a later agreement lawfully restores any group functions.\n\n### 3. Return eligible people to outside placements\n\n**PROPOSED:** Those cleared can leave while responsible leaders remain restricted. Gives followers stakes; some may choose Konrad from genuine attachment or fear.\n\n### 4. Offer supervised transition with revocable limited coordination\n\n**PROPOSED:** The group can manage practical winding-down without political sovereignty. Creates the specific delegation Samuel exploits; must not legalize coercive reproductive institutions.\n\n## Targeted follow-up questions\n\n- What does an ordinary follower lose by following Konrad?\n- Who hears the real exit terms?\n- What personal warning does Konrad knowingly disregard?\n\n## Scene test\n\n**Non-canon situation:** A senior follower has an approved independent placement; Konrad persuades them to abandon it for one final demonstration.\n\nRecord what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.\n\n## Adversarial questions\n\n- How can one leader’s refusal bind people who never consented to remain?\n- Which established constraint would this answer break, and what evidence would reveal that break before the payoff?\n\n## Completion checklist\n\n- [ ] Answer the central question in the author's own words.\n- [ ] Identify the chosen possibility, a modified combination, or a different answer; explain rejected tradeoffs.\n- [ ] Resolve or explicitly defer prerequisites 02, 03, 08.\n- [ ] Run the scene test above and state the consequence for the people involved.\n- [ ] Answer the adversarial challenge without granting unexplained knowledge or authority.\n- [ ] Record what remains working, proposed, or unresolved.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit author acceptance before updating canon or workflow progress.\n- [ ] Trace the accepted answer through the affected notes and rebuild both projections.\n\n## Answer and decision record\n\n```text\nModule: 09 · Great War defeat and refusal to exit\nGate: What exactly would lawful exit have done to Konrad’s authority and to the people under him?\nState: DRAFT / PROPOSED / AUTHOR-ACCEPTED / REJECTED / DEFERRED\nAuthor answer (verbatim):\nExact restatement:\nSelected option or new answer:\nWhy this tradeoff:\nRejected alternatives and reasons:\nPrerequisites resolved / deferred:\nScene test: choices, permissions, evidence, cost:\nAdversarial result:\nRemaining uncertainty:\nExplicit acceptance wording and date:\nAffected notes updated:\nQA decision reference:\nWorkflow task and macro-depth effect:\nWebsite rebuild and verification:\n```\n\n## Notes and website sections affected\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/Konrad Fitzgerald]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Participant Governance and Command Rules]]\n\n- Public atlas: `docs/timeline.html`, the matching source in `05 Public/Atlas/`, and the workshop projection.\n- Development Explorer: the relevant topic view, this source packet, and linked evidence/decision records.\n- [[07 QA/Decisions]], [[07 QA/Questions]], and [[07 Coordination/Weekly Synthesis/CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE]]. Update [[07 Coordination/CURRENT-PICKUP]] and the current task only if the author accepts a workflow-relevant decision.\n",
      "html": "<h3 id=\"09-great-war-defeat-and-refusal-to-exit\">09 · Great War defeat and refusal to exit</h3>\n<h4 id=\"purpose\">Purpose</h4>\n<p>Make the historical hinge a real choice with a defined lawful alternative.</p>\n<p>This packet supports the existing Story Completion Workflow. It does not advance a checklist or settle canon. All alternatives below are PROPOSED; the gate is OPEN. Central synthesis: Astra, reviewed for integration on September 5.</p>\n<h4 id=\"relevant-source-notes\">Relevant source notes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/01%20Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05%20-%20Integrated%20Foundation%20Audit%20and%20Workshop%20Build.md\">2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Characters/Konrad%20Fitzgerald.md\">Konrad Fitzgerald</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Systems/Participant%20Governance%20and%20Command%20Rules.md\">Participant Governance and Command Rules</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"confirmed-facts-and-current-working-constraints\">Confirmed facts and current working constraints</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Konrad’s experiment should end after defeat.</li>\n<li>He chooses continued participation and reactivation to vindicate his ideology and daemon.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These constraints inherit their source status. A working physical model, timing estimate, or accepted macro constraint does not establish every implementation detail.</p>\n<h4 id=\"unresolved-gaps-and-contradictions\">Unresolved gaps and contradictions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Exit destination and sentence; individual versus collective choice; ability to refuse while remaining contained.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"prerequisite-decisions\">Prerequisite decisions</h4>\n<p>Modules: 02, 03, 08. Read their accepted results before closing this gate. Open prerequisites can be explored provisionally, but do not mark dependent choices final. Module numbers are topic IDs; use the dependency order in the workshop index.</p>\n<h4 id=\"central-author-gate\">Central author gate</h4>\n<blockquote>What exactly would lawful exit have done to Konrad’s authority and to the people under him?</blockquote>\n<p>Ask this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.</p>\n<h4 id=\"possibilities-and-tradeoffs\">Possibilities and tradeoffs</h4>\n<h5 id=\"1-end-command-continue-individual-review-elsewhere\">1. End command, continue individual review elsewhere</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Konrad leaves his governance role and faces ordinary adjudication; followers receive separate assessments. Clear distinction from freedom or absolution; requires another holding context.</p>\n<h5 id=\"2-disband-faction-jurisdiction-retain-bounded-personal-participation\">2. Disband faction jurisdiction, retain bounded personal participation</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Konrad could remain as an individual but rejects loss of corporate authority. Concentrates motive on domination; explain how a later agreement lawfully restores any group functions.</p>\n<h5 id=\"3-return-eligible-people-to-outside-placements\">3. Return eligible people to outside placements</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Those cleared can leave while responsible leaders remain restricted. Gives followers stakes; some may choose Konrad from genuine attachment or fear.</p>\n<h5 id=\"4-offer-supervised-transition-with-revocable-limited-coordination\">4. Offer supervised transition with revocable limited coordination</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> The group can manage practical winding-down without political sovereignty. Creates the specific delegation Samuel exploits; must not legalize coercive reproductive institutions.</p>\n<h4 id=\"targeted-follow-up-questions\">Targeted follow-up questions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>What does an ordinary follower lose by following Konrad?</li>\n<li>Who hears the real exit terms?</li>\n<li>What personal warning does Konrad knowingly disregard?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"scene-test\">Scene test</h4>\n<p><strong>Non-canon situation:</strong> A senior follower has an approved independent placement; Konrad persuades them to abandon it for one final demonstration.</p>\n<p>Record what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.</p>\n<h4 id=\"adversarial-questions\">Adversarial…5087 tokens truncated…ich single action changes Samuel’s authority when Konrad reactivates the group?\n\nAsk this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.\n\n## Possibilities and tradeoffs\n\n### 1. Parent-jurisdiction registration\n\n**PROPOSED:** Konrad registers an apparently separate domain as a child of Samuel’s existing sphere. Clean hierarchy; danger is overbroad automatic inheritance unless protected domains stay explicit.\n\n### 2. Delegated infrastructure administration\n\n**PROPOSED:** Konrad delegates restoration services while retaining political authority; administrator visibility enables later compromise. Plausible gradual capture; the legal distinction must matter in scenes.\n\n### 3. Shared emergency coordination mandate\n\n**PROPOSED:** A crisis authorizes Samuel across several domains temporarily; dependencies survive the mandate. Strong political causality; avoid emergency-rule cliché and explain failed expiry.\n\n### 4. Negotiated arbitration priority\n\n**PROPOSED:** Conflicts between the two domains go through Samuel’s earlier Primary standing. Preserves genuine Konrad authority; slow bureaucratic leverage needs one decisive scene and protected appeal.\n\n## Targeted follow-up questions\n\n- What record proves the exact changed permission?\n- What can Konrad still refuse afterward?\n- Can resetting credentials end access while leaving leaked secrets, coerced relationships and false records behind?\n\n## Scene test\n\n**Non-canon situation:** Konrad completes a restoration step to activate his lineage archive; an innocuous authority line later becomes the historical exhibit the inner circle recognizes.\n\nRecord what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.\n\n## Adversarial questions\n\n- If the lock is easily explainable now, why could Konrad not verify it then—and why did oversight allow misrepresentation?\n- Which established constraint would this answer break, and what evidence would reveal that break before the payoff?\n\n## Completion checklist\n\n- [ ] Answer the central question in the author's own words.\n- [ ] Identify the chosen possibility, a modified combination, or a different answer; explain rejected tradeoffs.\n- [ ] Resolve or explicitly defer prerequisites 07, 09, 10.\n- [ ] Run the scene test above and state the consequence for the people involved.\n- [ ] Answer the adversarial challenge without granting unexplained knowledge or authority.\n- [ ] Record what remains working, proposed, or unresolved.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit author acceptance before updating canon or workflow progress.\n- [ ] Trace the accepted answer through the affected notes and rebuild both projections.\n\n## Answer and decision record\n\n```text\nModule: 11 · Exact takeover lock\nGate: Which single action changes Samuel’s authority when Konrad reactivates the group?\nState: DRAFT / PROPOSED / AUTHOR-ACCEPTED / REJECTED / DEFERRED\nAuthor answer (verbatim):\nExact restatement:\nSelected option or new answer:\nWhy this tradeoff:\nRejected alternatives and reasons:\nPrerequisites resolved / deferred:\nScene test: choices, permissions, evidence, cost:\nAdversarial result:\nRemaining uncertainty:\nExplicit acceptance wording and date:\nAffected notes updated:\nQA decision reference:\nWorkflow task and macro-depth effect:\nWebsite rebuild and verification:\n```\n\n## Notes and website sections affected\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Participant Governance and Command Rules]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/Konrad Fitzgerald]]\n\n- Public atlas: `docs/faction.html`, the matching source in `05 Public/Atlas/`, and the workshop projection.\n- Development Explorer: the relevant topic view, this source packet, and linked evidence/decision records.\n- [[07 QA/Decisions]], [[07 QA/Questions]], and [[07 Coordination/Weekly Synthesis/CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE]]. Update [[07 Coordination/CURRENT-PICKUP]] and the current task only if the author accepts a workflow-relevant decision.\n\n## Blocking identity discrepancy\n\nSC-001 Question 5 names Samuel Jr. in the activation-related government takeover; current character/history notes place Samuel and George in the prewar attempt and Samuel Jr. later. Confirm the actor before locking the permission sequence. Do not silently correct an accepted task packet.\n",
      "html": "<h3 id=\"11-exact-takeover-lock\">11 · Exact takeover lock</h3>\n<h4 id=\"purpose\">Purpose</h4>\n<p>Choose one legible hinge that grants durable advantage without owning people.</p>\n<p>This packet supports the existing Story Completion Workflow. It does not advance a checklist or settle canon. All alternatives below are PROPOSED; the gate is OPEN. Central synthesis: Astra, reviewed for integration on September 5.</p>\n<h4 id=\"relevant-source-notes\">Relevant source notes</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/01%20Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05%20-%20Integrated%20Foundation%20Audit%20and%20Workshop%20Build.md\">2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Systems/Participant%20Governance%20and%20Command%20Rules.md\">Participant Governance and Command Rules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Characters/Konrad%20Fitzgerald.md\">Konrad Fitzgerald</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"confirmed-facts-and-current-working-constraints\">Confirmed facts and current working constraints</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Negotiated Primary is tiered alpha status, not blanket sovereignty.</li>\n<li>Konrad voluntarily reactivates systems; the exact lock, weighting and reset limit are unresolved.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These constraints inherit their source status. A working physical model, timing estimate, or accepted macro constraint does not establish every implementation detail.</p>\n<h4 id=\"unresolved-gaps-and-contradictions\">Unresolved gaps and contradictions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Action; jurisdiction; scope; consent; immutable record; reason reversal cannot undo damage.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"prerequisite-decisions\">Prerequisite decisions</h4>\n<p>Modules: 07, 09, 10. Read their accepted results before closing this gate. Open prerequisites can be explored provisionally, but do not mark dependent choices final. Module numbers are topic IDs; use the dependency order in the workshop index.</p>\n<h4 id=\"central-author-gate\">Central author gate</h4>\n<blockquote>Which single action changes Samuel’s authority when Konrad reactivates the group?</blockquote>\n<p>Ask this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.</p>\n<h4 id=\"possibilities-and-tradeoffs\">Possibilities and tradeoffs</h4>\n<h5 id=\"1-parent-jurisdiction-registration\">1. Parent-jurisdiction registration</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Konrad registers an apparently separate domain as a child of Samuel’s existing sphere. Clean hierarchy; danger is overbroad automatic inheritance unless protected domains stay explicit.</p>\n<h5 id=\"2-delegated-infrastructure-administration\">2. Delegated infrastructure administration</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Konrad delegates restoration services while retaining political authority; administrator visibility enables later compromise. Plausible gradual capture; the legal distinction must matter in scenes.</p>\n<h5 id=\"3-shared-emergency-coordination-mandate\">3. Shared emergency coordination mandate</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> A crisis authorizes Samuel across several domains temporarily; dependencies survive the mandate. Strong political causality; avoid emergency-rule cliché and explain failed expiry.</p>\n<h5 id=\"4-negotiated-arbitration-priority\">4. Negotiated arbitration priority</h5>\n<p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> Conflicts between the two domains go through Samuel’s earlier Primary standing. Preserves genuine Konrad authority; slow bureaucratic leverage needs one decisive scene and protected appeal.</p>\n<h4 id=\"targeted-follow-up-questions\">Targeted follow-up questions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>What record proves the exact changed permission?</li>\n<li>What can Konrad still refuse afterward?</li>\n<li>Can resetting credentials end access while leaving leaked secrets, coerced relationships and false records behind?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"scene-test\">Scene test</h4>\n<p><strong>Non-canon situation:</strong> Konrad completes a restoration step to activate his lineage archive; an innocuous authority line later becomes the historical exhibit the inner circle recognizes.</p>\n<p>Record what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.</p>\n<h4 id=\"adversarial-questions\">Adversarial questions</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>If the lock is easily explainable now, why could Konrad not verify it then—and why did oversight allow misrepresentation?</li>\n<li>Which established constraint would this answer break, and what evidence would reveal that break before the payoff?</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"completion-checklist\">Completion checklist</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>☐ Answer the central question in the author&#x27;s own words.</li>\n<li>☐ Identify the chosen possibility, a modified combination, or a different answer; explain rejected tradeoffs.</li>\n<li>☐ Resolve or explicitly defer prerequisites 07, 09, 10.</li>\n<li>☐ Run the scene test above and state the consequence for the people involved.</li>\n<li>☐ Answer the adversarial challenge without granting unexplained knowledge or authority.</li>\n<li>☐ Record what remains working, proposed, or unresolved.</li>\n<li>☐ Obtain explicit author acceptance before updating canon or workflow progress.</li>\n<li>☐ Trace the accepted answer through the affected notes and rebuild both projections.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"answer-and-decision-record\">Answer and decision record</h4>\n<pre><code>Module: 11 · Exact takeover lock\nGate: Which single action changes Samuel’s authority when Konrad reactivates the group?\nState: DRAFT / PROPOSED / AUTHOR-ACCEPTED / REJECTED / DEFERRED\nAuthor answer (verbatim):\nExact restatement:\nSelected option or new answer:\nWhy this tradeoff:\nRejected alternatives and reasons:\nPrerequisites resolved / deferred:\nScene test: choices, permissions, evidence, cost:\nAdversarial result:\nRemaining uncertainty:\nExplicit acceptance wording and date:\nAffected notes updated:\nQA decision reference:\nWorkflow task and macro-depth effect:\nWebsite rebuild and verification:</code></pre>\n<h4 id=\"notes-and-website-sections-affected\">Notes and website sections affected</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/01%20Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05%20-%20Integrated%20Foundation%20Audit%20and%20Workshop%20Build.md\">2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Systems/Participant%20Governance%20and%20Command%20Rules.md\">Participant Governance and Command Rules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/02%20Story/Characters/Konrad%20Fitzgerald.md\">Konrad Fitzgerald</a></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Public atlas: <code>docs/faction.html</code>, the matching source in <code>05 Public/Atlas/</code>, and the workshop projection.</li>\n<li>Development Explorer: the relevant topic view, this source packet, and linked evidence/decision records.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20QA/Decisions.md\">Decisions</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20QA/Questions.md\">Questions</a>, and <a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20Coordination/Weekly%20Synthesis/CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE.md\">CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE</a>. Update <a href=\"https://github.com/cubixmeow-commits/seeds-of-the-throne/blob/main/07%20Coordination/CURRENT-PICKUP.md\">CURRENT-PICKUP</a> and the current task only if the author accepts a workflow-relevant decision.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"blocking-identity-discrepancy\">Blocking identity discrepancy</h4>\n<p>SC-001 Question 5 names Samuel Jr. in the activation-related government takeover; current character/history notes place Samuel and George in the prewar attempt and Samuel Jr. later. Confirm the actor before locking the permission sequence. Do not silently correct an accepted task packet.</p>"
