      "markdown": "---\ntype: workshop-module\nstatus: proposed-options-author-gate-open\nmodule: 19\ntitle: Accountability, consequences and final placement\ngate: What decisions close Book One for individuals, the criminal structures and the institution itself?\nprerequisites: 03, 08, 12, 14, 18\nupdated: 2026-09-05\n---\n\n# 19 · Accountability, consequences and final placement\n\n## Purpose\n\nPrevent either last-minute cooperation or ancestry from determining total human worth.\n\nThis packet supports the existing Story Completion Workflow. It does not advance a checklist or settle canon. All alternatives below are PROPOSED; the gate is OPEN. Central synthesis: Astra, reviewed for integration on September 5.\n\n## Relevant source notes\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/The Other Son - Contingency and Survival]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/George White - The Collapse of the Lie]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Integration and Scoring]]\n\n## Confirmed facts and current working constraints\n\n- People may be victims and perpetrators at different times.\n- The process assesses bonded effectiveness and concrete conduct; descendants inherit no guilt.\n\nThese constraints inherit their source status. A working physical model, timing estimate, or accepted macro constraint does not establish every implementation detail.\n\n## Unresolved gaps and contradictions\n\n- Sanctions; remedies; review; safe exit; future leadership limits; leaders’ accountability.\n\n## Prerequisite decisions\n\nModules: 03, 08, 12, 14, 18. Read their accepted results before closing this gate. Open prerequisites can be explored provisionally, but do not mark dependent choices final. Module numbers are topic IDs; use the dependency order in the workshop index.\n\n## Central author gate\n\n> What decisions close Book One for individuals, the criminal structures and the institution itself?\n\nAsk this question alone during actual use. Do not ask every follow-up at once.\n\n## Possibilities and tradeoffs\n\n### 1. Separate containment, responsibility and placement findings\n\n**PROPOSED:** One person can be protected from Samuel, held responsible for harm and given a limited future. Most nuanced; needs clear presentation to avoid bureaucratic overload.\n\n### 2. Provisional outcomes with enforceable conditions\n\n**PROPOSED:** Immediate safety and bounded opportunities precede later review. Preserves uncertainty and realism; Book One still needs a satisfying irreversible result.\n\n### 3. Restitution and testimony alongside restricted authority\n\n**PROPOSED:** Cooperation matters because it repairs specific harm, not because it buys innocence. Human consequences; victims must not be required to forgive or participate.\n\n### 4. Institutional accountability as a parallel verdict\n\n**PROPOSED:** Leaders accept constraints and remedies for process failures alongside criminal findings. Strong thematic closure; do not falsely equalize all actors’ conduct.\n\n## Targeted follow-up questions\n\n- Can a brilliant bond be denied authority because its human abused power?\n- What does a coerced facilitator owe those later harmed?\n- Can the organization retain cultural association while coercive command is dismantled?\n\n## Scene test\n\n**Non-canon situation:** A descendant declines to become a public symbol of liberation; the final arrangement protects that refusal even though it would make the presentation less persuasive.\n\nRecord what each person wants, can know, can refuse, and can actually change. Name the observable difference between the selected alternatives.\n\n## Adversarial questions\n\n- Does one final good decision erase decades of harm, or does it change the future while leaving the past accountable?\n- Which established constraint would this answer break, and what evidence would reveal that break before the payoff?\n\n## Completion checklist\n\n- [ ] Answer the central question in the author's own words.\n- [ ] Identify the chosen possibility, a modified combination, or a different answer; explain rejected tradeoffs.\n- [ ] Resolve or explicitly defer prerequisites 03, 08, 12, 14, 18.\n- [ ] Run the scene test above and state the consequence for the people involved.\n- [ ] Answer the adversarial challenge without granting unexplained knowledge or authority.\n- [ ] Record what remains working, proposed, or unresolved.\n- [ ] Obtain explicit author acceptance before updating canon or workflow progress.\n- [ ] Trace the accepted answer through the affected notes and rebuild both projections.\n\n## Answer and decision record\n\n```text\nModule: 19 · Accountability, consequences and final placement\nGate: What decisions close Book One for individuals, the criminal structures and the institution itself?\nState: DRAFT / PROPOSED / AUTHOR-ACCEPTED / REJECTED / DEFERRED\nAuthor answer (verbatim):\nExact restatement:\nSelected option or new answer:\nWhy this tradeoff:\nRejected alternatives and reasons:\nPrerequisites resolved / deferred:\nScene test: choices, permissions, evidence, cost:\nAdversarial result:\nRemaining uncertainty:\nExplicit acceptance wording and date:\nAffected notes updated:\nQA decision reference:\nWorkflow task and macro-depth effect:\nWebsite rebuild and verification:\n```\n\n## Notes and website sections affected\n\n- [[01 Sessions/Daily/2026-09-05 - Integrated Foundation Audit and Workshop Build]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/The Other Son - Contingency and Survival]]\n- [[02 Story/Characters/George White - The Collapse of the Lie]]\n- [[02 Story/Systems/Integration and Scoring]]\n\n- Public atlas: `docs/colonization.html`, the matching source in `05 Public/Atlas/`, and the workshop projection.\n- Development Explorer: the relevant topic view, this source packet, and linked evidence/decision records.\n- [[07 QA/Decisions]], [[07 QA/Questions]], and [[07 Coordination/Weekly Synthesis/CURRENT-WEEK-INTAKE]]. Update [[07 Coordination/CURRENT-PICKUP]] and the current task only if the author accepts a workflow-relevant decision.\n",
